      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "William Heath Davis founded New Town in 1850, which later evolved into the Gaslamp Quarter we know today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://gaslamp.org/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Around 1970, San Diego shifted toward urban development and historic preservation, restoring landmarks like the Buel‑Town Building, now the Old Spaghetti Factory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.govisitsandiego.com/things-to-do/history/history-of-gaslamp-quarter/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Gaslamp Museum at the Davis‑Horton House is the headquarters of the Gaslamp Quarter Historical Foundation, preserving the district’s past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
